# THE ONE FACT THE LTS TOOLING CANNOT DERIVE: which release line, if any, is the
# supported long-term-support line right now.
#
# Read by hack/lts.sh (and through it the backport workflow and the LTS upgrade
# drill). One supported LTS line at a time, 18 months, security and critical fixes
# only; docs/docs/deployment/lts-policy.md is the public statement of the promise.
#
#   current-lts: none     no line is designated; the backport workflow proposes
#                         nothing and the drill refuses to run
#   current-lts: X.Y      the line X.Y is the LTS line. Its branch is
#                         release-X.Y-lts, cut from the X.Y.0 tag, and every patch
#                         release of the line is tagged from that branch
#
# DECLARED, NOT INFERRED: designating a line is a decision a maintainer takes after
# the line has soaked, so it is written down here by a pull request and not guessed
# from the tag list. Designating a line is the only edit this file ever needs.
current-lts: none
